From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tarwin Stroh-Spijer <tarwin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] h2: client: a request sent with END_STREAM is half-closed at once

A body-less client request goes out as a HEADERS frame carrying
END_STREAM, but lws_h2_client_handshake() left the stream OPEN, and only a
later POLLOUT pass moved it to HALF_CLOSED_LOCAL.  A server answering
before that pass (anything fast, eg on loopback) had its END_STREAM move
the stream to HALF_CLOSED_REMOTE, which the POLLOUT pass then overwrote
with HALF_CLOSED_LOCAL: the stream never reached CLOSED, the transaction
never completed and the request hung until its timeout.

Set HALF_CLOSED_LOCAL as the HEADERS go out when they carried END_STREAM,
and never move a CLOSED stream back in the POLLOUT pass.

The second part is a subset of upstream 4f8d4fdee (main, "h2: a write to
a stream ended both ways fails"), which also moves HALF_CLOSED_REMOTE to
CLOSED there; that is left out, since it also changes when server streams
close.  The first part is not upstream: main still leaves the stream OPEN.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
  lib/roles/h2/http2.c  |   10 +++++++++-
  lib/roles/h2/ops-h2.c |    3 ++-
  2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/roles/h2/http2.c b/lib/roles/h2/http2.c
--- a/lib/roles/h2/http2.c
+++ b/lib/roles/h2/http2.c
@@ -3039,7 +3048,15 @@ lws_h2_client_handshake(struct lws *wsi)
 	if (lws_h2_update_peer_txcredit(wsi, (unsigned int)wsi->mux.my_sid, n))
 		return 1;
 
-	lws_h2_state(wsi, LWS_H2_STATE_OPEN);
+	/*
+	 * If END_STREAM went out on the HEADERS, the stream is half-closed
+	 * from here on.  Leaving it OPEN until a later POLLOUT pass lets a
+	 * fast peer's END_STREAM arrive first and move it to HALF_CLOSED_REMOTE,
+	 * which that pass then overwrites with HALF_CLOSED_LOCAL, so the
+	 * stream never reaches CLOSED and the transaction never completes
+	 */
+	lws_h2_state(wsi, wsi->h2.send_END_STREAM ?
+			  LWS_H2_STATE_HALF_CLOSED_LOCAL : LWS_H2_STATE_OPEN);
 	lwsi_set_state(wsi, LRS_ESTABLISHED);
 
 	if (wsi->mux.my_sid == 1) {
diff --git a/lib/roles/h2/ops-h2.c b/lib/roles/h2/ops-h2.c
--- a/lib/roles/h2/ops-h2.c
+++ b/lib/roles/h2/ops-h2.c
@@ -1508,7 +1522,8 @@ rops_perform_user_POLLOUT_h2(struct lws *wsi)
 			lws_close_free_wsi(w, LWS_CLOSE_STATUS_NOSTATUS,
 					   "h2 pollout handle");
 		} else {
-			 if (w->h2.send_END_STREAM)
+			 if (w->h2.send_END_STREAM &&
+			     w->h2.h2_state != LWS_H2_STATE_CLOSED)
 				lws_h2_state(w, LWS_H2_STATE_HALF_CLOSED_LOCAL);
 
 #if defined(LWS_WITH_CLIENT)
-- 
2.55.0.windows.3

